  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a full 92-minute set at Ottobar in Baltimore, Maryland, on April 14, 2011, capturing 23 songs for this recording [1][6]. This show is the 161st in the Internet Archive’s collection for the band, following a previous appearance at the Wexner Center on April 11, 2011 [6]. The setlist includes tracks like “Liza Forever Minnelli,” “Southwood Plantation Road,” and “Dinu Lapatti’s Bones,” alongside rare performances of “Family Happiness” and “Outer Scorpion Squadron” [1][6]. Notably, “Cheshire County” appears here for the first time in 48 archived shows, a gap of 1,291 days [1][6]. The recording, taped and transferred by breathmint, includes two encores [1]. The uploader notes that a recorder mic input issue caused some loss of stereo sound, which was addressed by replacing affected sections with dual mono [1]. While most audio fixes occurred between songs, some portions were removed to clean up the track [1]. Listener bonkersmonkers recalls the enthusiastic crowd, though they note the audience seemed less receptive to slower, then-new songs from the album *AED* [5]. Despite this, “Never Quite Free” shines through in the recording [5]. The set concludes with “The Best Ever Death Metal Band In Denton,” offering a complete snapshot of the night [1][6].",
